Z||000000||Scott_M||01-03-2001||10:35 PM||||I'm looking for the washer that goes on the EGR valve. The orignal is lost(not in the engine thank God) and the exhaust has already burned through two gaskets. I've seen on the forum that the replacement EGR's come with an assortment of washers and I was wondering if someone out there could sell me an extra.Or if I could get it at a hardware store. The EGR is numbered<BR>CFJ 17084743<BR>269 614<BR>Any help would be appreciated.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000001||theogre||01-04-2001||08:18 PM||||If you find another washer, or replace the EGR, read the emissions notes in my cave about how to install it. Then you won't keep loosing them.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-04-2001||08:39 PM||||you'd be lucky if you could find one in a hardware store, more in likely it would be a machine bushing, not a regular washer.  either way, you might as well try it for lack of a better thing, possibly you could grind it down to fit the diameter, and then make sure it was flush enough.  You have to use a punch and a hammer to hold the washer in place, there should have been some instructions that came with your valve.  If you cant find one, I would be able to send you one of mine (it wont be the correct washer for the fiero, but it will be very close.) that I have extra, if I could find it.  I'd probably be able to get it in the mail on monday, if you cant find one this weekend.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Scott_M||01-05-2001||08:31 PM||||Thanks guys. I'll see what I can find at home depot. ||||reg||1
